      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "The navigate algorithm sets the referrer policy, HTTPS state, and CSP list from the response that is (sort of) passed in to the navigate algorithm. So this seems like the right way to go.\n\nThe \"reload override flag\" and \"reload override buffer\" seem like things that are not part of a response, i.e. if we refactor the navigate algorithm, it will take a parameter list that looks something like (browsingContext, resource, exceptions enabled flag, reload override flag, reload override buffer). But referrer policy/CSP list/HTTPS state will be part of the response still.\n\n(Not sure about \"override URL\"; it could go either way.)\n",
